<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Federal Convention (German Confederation)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1815">1815</a>–<a href="/years/1866">1866</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Federal Diet of the German Confederation, Bundesversammlung, Frankfurt Federal Diet</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Federal Convention, usually called the Federal Diet, was the only central institution of the German Confederation from 1815 to 1866. It sat in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a>, in the Thurn und Taxis palace, as a permanent congress of envoys from the member states, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> presiding. It enforced repressive measures such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlsbad-decrees">Carlsbad Decrees</a>, and its vote to mobilise against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> in 1866 led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-prussian-war">Austro-Prussian War</a> and the end of the confederation.</p></div>
